pi-coding-agent for Debian
=========================

Source format: 3.0 (native).

Network requirement
--------------------
The build needs network access to the npm registry. Two `npm install` calls
fetch packages:

  * override_dh_auto_configure: `npm install --ignore-scripts` hydrates the
    workspace dev toolchain (tsgo, shx, vitest, ...).
  * debian/stage: `npm install --omit=dev --ignore-scripts` installs the
    third-party runtime deps of @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent into the
    staging tree.

`node_modules/` and the compiled `packages/*/dist` trees are therefore not
part of the source package (excluded via debian/source/options); they are
regenerated during the build.

Near-offline builds
-------------------
To build without live network access, pre-populate the npm cache first from a
networked machine, then point the build at it:

    npm install --ignore-scripts          # warm ~/.npm/_cacache
    # copy ~/.npm/_cacache onto the build host, then:
    HOME=<home-with-cache> dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

Both `npm install` invocations resolve from the cache when the registry is
unreachable.

Tests
-----
override_dh_auto_test does not run the upstream suite. The suite needs Node's
TypeScript stripper (tui: `node --test *.ts`; ai: a `node --eval` probe over
.ts sources), which Debian's nodejs is built without (ERR_NO_TYPESCRIPT). A
`pi --version` smoke test runs instead; the full suite runs in upstream CI.
